    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a `capacityWarning` response flag that is `true` when an owner's city already holds **40\u201349** owners (approaching the per-city limit of 50). The hard rejection at 50 is unchanged.\n\nFollowing the codebase's existing pattern for derived response flags (`bulkSignupWarning`, `possibleDuplicate` \u2014 computed at response time, not stored), the changes were:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the new `capacityWarning` boolean (read-only) on the owner schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets a `setCapacityWarning`.\n\n2. **`CityCapacity.java`** (new helper) \u2014 extracted the per-city counting logic and the `MAX_PER_CITY = 50` constant into a shared helper, adding `WARN_FROM = 40` and `warningFor(owner, repo)` returning `count >= 40 && count < 50`. This single-sources the capacity limit for both the hard check and the warning.\n\n3. **`CheckCityCapacity.java`** \u2014 reduced to a single-public-method step (per the AGENTS.md rule) that delegates counting/limit to `CityCapacity`; the 409 rejection behavior is unchanged.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 marked `capacityWarning` as `ignore = true` (set manually, like the other flags).\n\n5. **`RespondWithOwner`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, `CheckIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 set the flag via `CityCapacity.warningFor(...)` on GET, POST-create, and idempotent-replay responses, consistent with how the sibling flags are set.\n\nA city at exactly 50 (full) reads as at-capacity rather than \"approaching\", so it warns `false`. The new `AcceptanceTest.coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\nI initially put `warningFor` as a second public method on `CheckCityCapacity`, which failed at startup because OfficeFloor requires exactly one public method per step class \u2014 hence the extraction into `CityCapacity`.",
